WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:04.480
Let's see how we can outline, reorder,

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.120
and re generally reorganize the

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.080
structure of our site in hacks.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.559
For this, we have two major ways that we

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:16.240
can work. One is this pencil just off

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.560
the side of the active page that says

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.000
outline actions. The other is the

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.480
outline of the site.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.640
Let's start with small incontext

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.720
actions. So I go to outline actions and

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.440
from here can see I can add a page

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.840
underneath this one. Move this page up

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.520
and down relative to its siblings indent

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.200
out or jump it somewhere else. There's

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.920
also a shortcut to the open site outline

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.000
which is the same as if we clicked on

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.680
this button.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.960
So first let's outdent this page and

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.520
we'll see that it moves it outside of

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.840
this parent page.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.120
From there, I could move it up.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.000
I could switch to this other page that

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.479
was previously the parent. Opening the

00:01:06.479 --> 00:01:09.200
outline again, I could say indent. And

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.680
now we've effectively reordered this

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.799
little part of our outline.

00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:17.280
I could take new page and indent, which

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.720
then moves it under add images. And if I

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.880
take one of these pages and move it up,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.000
all the children come with it.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.080
So another way that we could do that if

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.920
we have a bigger vision of bulk

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.680
operations that need to take place in

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.799
our outline going to the south out site

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:37.600
outline and structure tab. So from here

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.000
we can see all of our pages. We can

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:43.040
rapidly add a whole bunch of pages. We

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:46.079
can move these and nest them. Think of

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:47.680
this as more of a planning and

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.360
prototyping tool as well as duplicating

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.479
large structures. So, if I'm having a

00:01:54.479 --> 00:01:56.079
site, it's documentation,

00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:58.240
tutorial-based, an online course,

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.079
something of that nature, it might make

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:02.960
sense to craft a really good d uh

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:06.000
structure for my site. Duplicate that

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.720
structure. I can double click and rename

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.200
pages in bulk.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:18.400
I can tab to the next item

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.720
and rename those pages. I can move these

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.680
around just like I could before, but

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.760
those actions were instant. Whereas this

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.400
has a bit of planning involved.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.200
I hit save outline and this thing thing

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.360
will say, hey, I'm about to add 11 new

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.560
pages. Are you sure? Sure.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.720
And now we've got all of those pages

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.200
with the structure duplicating content

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:43.840
if it existed and then organized the way

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:45.840
we wanted it.
